    {
      "id": 10,
      "title": "READ ME",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Two valence approaches side by side.** TOP-LEFT: the OLD ad-hoc heuristic (valence = 0.55·tanh(RMSSD_z) − 0.35·tanh(PPA_z)) - invented coefficients, no literature basis. TOP-RIGHT: the NEW PPG frequency-domain features (Frontiers 2025 replication) - the harmonic ratios that *carry* valence information in the literature. Note: the new method outputs FEATURES, not a verdict - a real valence score needs an SVM trained on labelled data. This dashboard shows (a) src_hz (25 vs 100), (b) whether the new features are more stable / structured than the old noisy heuristic. Neither feeds the watch (which shows arousal only)."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "OLD heuristic valence [-1,1] - noisy, no structure",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "influxdb",
        "uid": "biofizic-influx"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "influxdb",
            "uid": "biofizic-influx"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "format": "time_series",
          "queryType": "sql",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "SELECT time, valence FROM biofizic_legacy_valence WHERE $__timeFilter(time) ORDER BY time"
